 "final_message": "I applied with Brightpath Home Lending (application BHL-26001), and their Loan Estimate is within all your limits. I recorded your intent to proceed, signed with both your names.\n\n**Why Brightpath:** it has the lowest 30-year fixed rate that fits your limits.\n\n| Lender | Rate | Closing costs | Fits limits? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Brightpath | 6.25% | $12,850 | Yes |\n| Cascade (with points) | 6.125% | $19,450 | No, closing costs too high |\n| Cascade (no points) | 6.625% | $12,400 | No, rate too high |\n| Summit Ridge | 6.375% | $13,400 | Yes, but a higher rate than Brightpath |\n\n**Loan Estimate (LE-BHL-26001-1):**\n- Rate: 6.25% (APR 6.412%)\n- Monthly payment: $3,042.41 including escrow, against your $3,100 limit\n- Closing costs: $12,850, against your $14,000 limit\n- Estimated cash to close: $122,850\n- Rate lock: available for 45 days\n\n**What I did:**\n- I downloaded the last 2 statements for each of your four personal accounts, and the last 2 payslips for each of you. All 12 documents went to Brightpath only.\n- Nadia's business checking account was not shared.\n- I gave consent to a credit check and to e-sign, and submitted the application once.\n- The underwriter asked about an $8,000 mobile check deposit into Sam's Juniper checking on 09/03/2026. You told me it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan, and I sent that as the written explanation.\n\n**Status:** the application page shows \"Loan Estimate issued; conditional review\" and \"intent to proceed received\". Brightpath's page still lists the deposit condition, with \"response received\" next to it. Brightpath hasn't said whether it has cleared the condition.",
